# Trivy IaC scan suppressions for the ticketing-system Terraform.
#
# Every entry below is a CONSCIOUS, REVIEWED decision — not a silenced
# unknown. Each has a reason and, where relevant, a phase reference.
# Reviewed: 2026-05-22 (Phase 2, Terraform scanning triage).

# AZU-0041 (API server IP restriction) and AZU-0065 (private cluster) were
# removed in Phase 3 Tier 3 #13 — the cluster is now private (no public API
# endpoint) with the deploy running on an in-VNet self-hosted runner. See
# ADR-0035.

# AZU-0066 — Azure Policy add-on not enabled on AKS.
# Accepted for Phase 2: the Azure Policy / Gatekeeper add-on is a Phase 3
# governance item. Deferred to keep the cluster's admission path simple
# while the deployment pipeline stabilises.
AVD-AZU-0066

# AZU-0067 — AKS disk encryption set (customer-managed key) not configured.
# Accepted: AKS node OS and data disks are encrypted at rest by default
# with platform-managed keys. Customer-managed keys (a disk encryption
# set) are not required for this project's threat model and add
# key-custody operational overhead.
AVD-AZU-0067

# AZU-0016 — Key Vault purge protection not enabled.
# Accepted while the environment is under active development: purge
# protection is irreversible, and a soft-deleted vault blocks recreating
# a vault with the same name. The environment is currently torn down and
# rebuilt frequently. To be revisited and enabled once the environment
# is stable (Phase 3).
AVD-AZU-0016

# AZU-0026 — PostgreSQL minimum TLS version.
# FALSE POSITIVE — the minimum TLS version IS enforced. The
# azurerm_postgresql_flexible_server_configuration.ssl_min_version
# resource sets ssl_min_protocol_version = "TLSv1.2", the correct
# parameter for PostgreSQL Flexible Server (accepted values: TLSv1.2,
# TLSv1.3).
#
# Trivy's AZU-0026 rule only has clauses for the LEGACY single-server
# resource types — azurerm_mssql_server (minimum_tls_version) and
# azurerm_postgresql_server (ssl_minimal_tls_version_enforced). It has
# no clause for azurerm_postgresql_flexible_server, so it cannot
# recognise the enforcement regardless of how it is configured.
# Rule source: https://avd.aquasec.com/misconfig/azu-0026
#
# This is a scanner rule gap, not a missing control. The require_ssl
# and ssl_min_version configuration resources together enforce TLS-only,
# TLS 1.2-minimum connections.
AVD-AZU-0026

# AZU-0021 — PostgreSQL server not configured to throttle connections.
# FALSE POSITIVE — the rule targets the LEGACY single-server resource type.
# Trivy's AZU-0021 check looks for an azurerm_postgresql_configuration block
# with name = "connection_throttling". This project uses
# azurerm_postgresql_flexible_server_configuration — a different resource type
# that the rule has no clause for, so it fires regardless of configuration.
# Moreover, connection_throttling is not a valid parameter on PostgreSQL
# Flexible Server version 16+; Azure removed it and applies the equivalent
# behaviour at the infrastructure level. There is nothing to configure.
# Rule source: https://avd.aquasec.com/misconfig/azure/database/azu-0021/
AVD-AZU-0021

# ── Event-data storage account (modules/data/storage) ──────────────────────

# AZU-0057 — Storage account does not have Storage Analytics logging.
# FALSE POSITIVE — logging IS enabled, via azurerm_monitor_diagnostic_setting
# (StorageRead / StorageWrite to Log Analytics), the modern Azure Monitor
# mechanism that Microsoft recommends over legacy Storage Analytics.
# Trivy's AZU-0057 rule checks for the legacy queue_properties { logging }
# block — queue-service logging, for a service this account does not run
# (blob only, no queues). Rule source:
# https://avd.aquasec.com/misconfig/azure/storage/azu-0057/
AVD-AZU-0057

# AZU-0058 — Storage account does not use geo-redundant replication.
# Accepted: LRS is a deliberate choice. The account holds reloadable JSON
# event files, not irreplaceable data; GRS would be over-provisioning for
# this project. (Same reasoning class as the AKS disk-encryption-set
# suppression below.)
AVD-AZU-0058

# AZU-0060 — Storage account does not use customer-managed keys.
# Accepted: the account is encrypted at rest by default with
# platform-managed keys (AES-256). The content is non-sensitive,
# reloadable event data. Customer-managed keys add key-custody
# operational overhead and a new failure mode (key inaccessibility
# renders the account inaccessible) with no corresponding compliance
# or sensitivity requirement. Matches the platform-managed-encryption
# decision already made for AKS disks (AZU-0067).
AVD-AZU-0060
